diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 2e02c9a..88cafa3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@ Open a quiz with at least one active question and select **Start a game**. Put t
 
 Select **Start** to open the first active question, **Finish** to show results, and **Next** to continue. Select **End quiz** after the last result. Players can change their pick until **Finish** and can return to the same game in the same browser without joining again. Every **Start a game** creates a separate game.
 
+## Award prizes
+
+Set **Number of winners** in the quiz’s **Settings** before starting a game (default: 3). Players get one point per correct final pick. The leaderboard appears after **End quiz**, ordered by points and then by the total time taken for correct picks. Phones show only their own place and points.
+
+Use **Top N** to award prizes in leaderboard order, or **Draw** to choose randomly among players tied on points at the prize cutoff. Players above the cutoff keep their prizes, and each draw is independent. Zero-point players never win. **Reset winners** clears all marks. The projector and phones update without a reload.
+
 ## Reuse or share a quiz
 
 On the quiz page, select **Export** and copy the JSON. On the destination Quizzy instance, open `/moderate`, select **Import quiz**, paste into **Quiz JSON**, and select **Import**. Import creates a separate quiz even if the title matches an existing one. If the JSON is invalid, the form keeps what you pasted so you can correct it and retry.
